:true,"_score_accruals":43.0,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.04829934773319521,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":100.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.05196345753834841,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":35.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.011175094269760932,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":35.5,"_gate_rev_durability":0.09131959933177858,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":70.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0167000867520424,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":29.7,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.026070094228329066,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":82.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.047571387972470375,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":20.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.097729996,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":65.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp operates as the bank holding company for Farmers & Merchants Bank of Central California that provides various banking services to businesses and individuals in the United States. The company provides deposit products, including checking, savings, money market, time certificates of deposit, and individual retirement accounts. It also offers a range of lending products, such as commercial, commercial and residential real estate, real estate construction, agribusiness, and consumer loans, as well as equipment leases and credit card services; commercial products, including term loans, lines of credit and other working capital financing, and letters of credit; and financing products, such as automobile financing, home improvement, and home equity lines of credit. In addition, the company provides specialized services that include credit card programs for merchants, lockbox and other collection services, account reconciliation, investment sweep, online account access, and electronic funds transfers through domestic and international wire and automated clearinghouse; online banking services; and investment products, such as mutual funds and annuities. Farmers & Merchants Bancorp was founded in 1916 and is headquartered in Lodi, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kent A. Steinwert | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 72 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 383 people. Revenue per employee of $634K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $252K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Farmers & Merchants Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.0B market cap on $243M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 47% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 40-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $97M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 40 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.8% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 24% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 56% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (FMCB) Could Be 46% Below Fair Value On Earnings Growth","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/farmers-merchants-bancorp-fmcb-could-002739237.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793060859.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.96,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Did Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (FMCB) Shares Climb Today?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/otc-fmcb/farmers-merchants-bancorp/news/why-did-farmers-merchants-bancorp-fmcb-shares-climb-today","date":"2026-10-23","timestamp":1792748421.507,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (OTCMKTS:FMCB) Announces Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/21/farmers-merchants-bancorp-otcmktsfmcb-announces-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-10-21","timestamp":1792581059.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp GAAP EPS of $36.75, revenue of $64.57M (FMCB:OTCMKTS)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4654835-farmers-and-merchants-bancorp-gaap-eps-of-36_75-revenue-of-64_57m","date":"2026-10-20","timestamp":1792522237.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (NASDAQ:FMAO) Stock Purchase Reported by Rep. Robert E. Latta","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/farmers-merchants-bancorp-nasdaqfmao-stock-purchase-reported-by-rep-robert-e-latta.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793948471.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Farmers & Merch